    "unit": 49,
    "title": "Balancing Formal and Informal Register",
    "title_ko": "격식·비격식 균형 맞추기",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Fluent speakers adjust register to the situation: formal for emails and presentations ('I would like to propose ...'), informal for chatting with friends ('Wanna grab lunch?'). Mixing registers inappropriately (too casual in a formal email, or overly stiff with friends) sounds unnatural.",
    "explanation_ko": "유창한 화자는 상황에 맞게 격식을 조정합니다: 이메일·발표에는 격식체('I would like to propose ...'), 친구와의 잡담에는 비격식체('Wanna grab lunch?'). 격식을 부적절하게 섞으면(격식체 이메일에 너무 캐주얼하거나, 친구에게 너무 딱딱하게) 부자연스럽게 들립니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I would like to propose an alternative approach.",
        "ko": "다른 접근 방식을 제안하고 싶습니다."
      },
      {
        "en": "Wanna grab lunch later?",
        "ko": "이따가 점심 먹을래?"
      },
      {
        "en": "Could we possibly reschedule?",
        "ko": "혹시 일정을 바꿀 수 있을까요?"
      }
    ]
  },
